<!-- ABOUT -->
<section id="about" class="alt">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <p class="section-label">About Me</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Structure, clarity,<br/>and follow-through.</h2>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-text fade-in">
        <p>I am a Project Support Officer and PMO Coordinator with a background spanning public health programme delivery and PMO support for digital transformation and health-service projects. I bring genuine public health expertise to health-sector stakeholder conversations, having coordinated multi-agency policy work with organisations including WHO, UNICEF, and USAID.</p>
        <p>I moved into PMO and project support work because I realised I am strongest in roles where I can bring structure, clarity, and coordination to a team. What draws me to PMO is that it sits at the centre of delivery — supporting progress in a practical way while working across people, processes, timelines, and stakeholder expectations.</p>
        <p>I am dependable, resourceful, and conscientious about the quality of my work. I take ownership, I follow through, and I do not like leaving things disorganised or unfinished. I work well in team environments but I am also comfortable taking initiative when something needs to be chased, clarified, or improved.</p>
        <p>I am actively seeking PMO Analyst, Project Support Officer, and Business Analyst roles across the UK and am open to relocation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-aside fade-in" style="transition-delay: 0.15s;">
        <div class="aside-block">
          <h4>Education</h4>
          <p>MPH Public Health — University of Wolverhampton (2023–2024)<br/>BSc (Hons) Biochemistry — Elizade University (2016–2020)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="aside-block">
          <h4>Currently Targeting</h4>
          <p>PMO Analyst · Project Support Officer · Business Analyst<br/>Open to relocation across the UK</p>
        </div>
        <div class="aside-block">
          <h4>Certifications in Progress</h4>
          <p>APM Project Management Qualification (PMQ)<br/>PRINCE2 Foundation</p>
        </div>
        <div class="aside-block">
          <h4>Based In</h4>
          <p>Wolverhampton, UK</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BOOKEASE -->
<section id="bookease" class="white">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <p class="section-label">Featured Project</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">BookEase — Digital Scheduling<br/>Platform</h2>

    <div class="project-narrative fade-in">
      <h3>Project Overview</h3>
      <p>BookEase was a web-based appointment scheduling system designed to help professionals manage client bookings efficiently using free, open-source plugins. Built on WordPress and integrating tools including Booking Calendar and Contact Form 7, the platform enabled calendar-based appointment booking, automated email notifications, client information collection, and manual payment tracking — giving small professional practices a lightweight but functional scheduling solution.</p>
      <p>The project ran over 22 weeks, spanning six functional teams and a 20+ member Agile team. I functioned as PMO Coordinator and de facto PMO Lead — owning governance, reporting, RAID management, document control, and meeting discipline end to end. I coordinated a suite of nine weekly governance reports, improved on-time submission from approximately 65% to 95%, managed 20–25 RAID items, reduced overdue actions from five to zero, and maintained 12 milestones and 12 deliverables in Microsoft Project and Jira. I supported exception reporting for three approved extensions and tracked a $9,000 project budget. Documentation standards I introduced were later adopted as templates for two other projects.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="artefacts-grid">

      <div class="artefact-card fade-in">
        <div class="artefact-icon">📊</div>
        <h3>Stakeholder Reporting &amp; Governance</h3>
        <p>Coordinated a suite of nine weekly governance reports across the 22-week project lifecycle. Introduced report allocation, template control, standard file naming, central folders, deadlines, and a governance calendar — improving on-time submission from approximately 65% to 95% and reducing missing reports to zero. Produced the weekly Highlight Report and RAG Status dashboard, distributed ahead of each stakeholder review cycle.</p>
        <span class="artefact-tag">Highlight Report V2.1</span>
        <span class="artefact-tag">RAG Status Report V2.2</span>
      </div>

      <div class="artefact-card rust fade-in" style="transition-delay:0.1s;">
        <div class="artefact-icon">⚠️</div>
        <h3>RAID Log &amp; Risk Management</h3>
        <p>Owned the RAID log throughout the project lifecycle, tracking 20–25 live risks, assumptions, issues, and dependencies with weekly triage. Assigned PMO ownership and escalation routes to each item, reducing overdue actions from five to zero. Flagged a BSA approval dependency early, communicating the resulting schedule risk to stakeholders. The RAID log fed directly into the Highlight Report and RAG dashboard, forming a consistent governance loop.</p>
        <span class="artefact-tag">RAID Log V2.2 (sample — Week 14)</span>
      </div>

      <div class="artefact-card peach fade-in" style="transition-delay:0.2s;">
        <div class="artefact-icon">📝</div>
        <h3>Meeting Minutes &amp; Action Management</h3>
        <p>Managed the meeting minutes function across at least three meetings per week throughout the project — assigning minute takers to each session, ensuring consistent structure and quality, and taking minutes directly where needed. Introduced a structured action-tracking and follow-up process. Same-day action logs were circulated to attendees. Minutes fed into the governance cycle, informing the Highlight Report and maintaining an audit trail of decisions across all project stages.</p>
        <span class="artefact-tag">BA Meeting Minutes V2.2 (sample — Week 13)</span>
      </div>

      <div class="artefact-card brown fade-in" style="transition-delay:0.3s;">
        <div class="artefact-icon">📅</div>
        <h3>Project Planning &amp; Delivery Tracking</h3>
        <p>Maintained 12 milestones and 12 deliverables in Microsoft Project across all four stages — Initiation, Define, Execute, and Closure — spanning 42 tasks with sequenced dependencies and resource assignments. Produced a weekly Checklist Report logging planned and actual dates and progress statuses. Escalated extension requirements before deadlines and supported exception reporting for two four-week extensions and a final two-week extension, helping maintain project continuity.</p>
        <span class="artefact-tag">MS Project Plan V3</span>
        <span class="artefact-tag">Checklist Report V2.2 (sample)</span>
      </div>

      <div class="artefact-card fade-in" style="transition-delay:0.1s;">
        <div class="artefact-icon">🔄</div>
        <h3>Retrospectives &amp; Lessons Learnt</h3>
        <p>Co-authored the weekly Lessons Learnt Report throughout the project, capturing areas for improvement and successes with impact ratings and future actions. At stage gate, lessons were consolidated into the End Stage Report — a formal governance document reviewing performance against time, cost, quality, scope, benefits, and risk — confirming Define Stage completion and authorising progression to Execute Stage.</p>
        <span class="artefact-tag">Lessons Learnt Report V2.2 (sample)</span>
        <span class="artefact-tag">End Stage Report V2.0 — Define Stage</span>
      </div>

      <div class="artefact-card rust fade-in" style="transition-delay:0.2s;">
        <div class="artefact-icon">📋</div>
        <h3>Requirements Support &amp; Document Control</h3>
